📑 HR Workforce Analytics Dashboard

📖 Business Summary
This project focuses on analyzing workforce-related employee data using Power BI dashboard reporting techniques. 
The dashboard was created to monitor employee distribution, workforce trends, salary insights, overtime patterns and job satisfaction analysis across departments using interactive HR analytics visualizations.

🎯 Objectives & Focus
- Monitor total workforce distribution across departments and job levels.
- Analyze employee salary patterns and workforce demographics.
- Track overtime trends and workforce allocation insights.
- Evaluate employee satisfaction and education background analysis.
- Develop interactive HR reporting dashboards for workforce monitoring.

🌍 Analysis Coverage
- Department-wise Analysis
- Workforce Distribution Analysis
- Salary Insights
- Employee Demographic Analysis
- Job Satisfaction Reporting
- Overtime Trend Analysis

📈 Performance Indicators
- Total Employees
- Male & Female Employee Count
- Promotion Analysis
- Retrenchment Analysis
- Average Salary
- Job Satisfaction Rating
- Overtime Distribution
- Employee Experience Analysis

📊 Dashboard Structure

📌 Workforce Overview
Focused on overall workforce monitoring and employee distribution analysis using KPI cards, donut charts and comparative visualizations.

📌 Employee Insights
Focused on employee salary analysis, education background, marital status and job satisfaction reporting using interactive Power BI visuals.

🏆 Key Insights
- Some departments showed higher employee concentration and overtime allocation trends.
- Workforce analysis highlighted differences in employee job levels and organizational distribution.
- Salary comparison visuals helped identify department-wise compensation patterns.
- Employee satisfaction and demographic insights supported HR reporting and workforce understanding.

